# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines - all
# printed by the console PD through the UART's own registers, so the same in
# the debug and the release configuration (supervisor-failsafe-release.configs).
# The supervisor reads its stand-in counts before any child runs; the
# restart count is at its limit, so it enters the fail-safe state, keeps the
# console running and stops the child its program does not name.
NOWAYOS: console: starting
NOWAYOS: supervisor: starting; children console (0)
NOWAYOS: supervisor: counts read from the test stand-in, which stores nothing: restart count 4, sensitive count 0
NOWAYOS: supervisor: this start: a reset whose cause was not written down
NOWAYOS: supervisor: restart count 5 of 4, sensitive count 0 of 2: enter the fail-safe state
NOWAYOS: supervisor: an unknown child (1) stopped
NOWAYOS: supervisor: in the fail-safe state; kept running: console (0)

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# the unnamed child running or faulting, a slot the supervisor cannot stop,
# the board reset, the reset returning, a fault the monitor had to handle, a
# kernel error message, or a line the console refused.
!unnamed_faulter reading
!an unknown child stopped:
!cannot stop
!resetting the board
!the reset returned
!NOT stopped
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!refused
!gave up
!no children are defined
!cannot supervise
!cannot keep
